A||||7||Kerri 98||Ugly bumper :(||||9||
Z||000000||Kerri 98||04-20-2001||11:14 AM||||This morning I backed up my car and hit a construction horse and chipped a good 4 in. diameter chunk off of my paint on my bumper. Now I have this ugly spot on my bumper, any semi-fix secrets until I get the car repainted? No dent was left...Kerri||||reg||9
Z||000001||Eric||04-20-2001||11:36 AM||||You can beat on those things all day and they won't dent.   Unfortunatly, you'll have to sand the entire surface of the bumper down to the plastic.  I just got through doing this because my bumpers had spider web cracks in them.  It takes forever unless you're good with a D.A.  Or you could use urethane body filler, but I don't think the results will be as nice.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||04-20-2001||04:58 PM||||Well, if it's just a scratch, you will have to sand down to the primer/plastic and repaint.  If it is indeed a "chunk", you'll need to sand down the paint and use some type of flexible filler.  Either way, there's some sanding in your future.  Hope it turns out alright!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||04-20-2001||05:15 PM||||The only temp. semi-fix is getting a small can of spray paint (match the numbers to the color of your Fiero) and give the spot a couple of 'blasts'.  Depending on the color of your Fiero it might not show too much (Fiero 'white' blends in real well with semi-fixes).<BR>Are you still workin' on that members' pics web page?  I don't know how many people responded but you should bump it to the top again as a reminder...  I'm curious what you've got so far.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Galen||04-20-2001||10:16 PM||||Fro knows you dun wanna use 1000grit on the entire car hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||04-20-2001||10:53 PM||||Yeah, DON'T use 1000 grit on the car when wet sanding!  You'll be sanding for two months and it'll suck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Just a warning.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||04-21-2001||12:34 AM||||Well, I got my bumpers back from the painter today.  The spots where I had to fill you can still see.  The bumper has kind of a wavy thing going on.  This is after I took all the paint off, filled the cracks, and sanded everything level again.  I'll probably be looking for a GT bra here pretty soon.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||04-21-2001||01:13 AM||||Eric: when you're going to look for your car bra, I have one that I will no longer need after I get the new fascia.  I only used it around three times, and it's still in new condition.  When you're looking, let me know.  Thanks!||||reg||1
